    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0556" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1264</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-25T12:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1917, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Near Cienfuegos today Collado, revolutionary leader, with 9 men taken, prisoners.
                    Also Colonel Carlos Roca. This is only band known to be operating in that
                    section.</p>
                <p>Among 20 others to surrender in Camaguey and Santa Clara Province were deserters
                    from army.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
